{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh3aUkWJtyEGgED39Ahm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HvbQBK8TfzVFPLkN3Ehi8E","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184651__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-184651; export TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp; echo '{\"name\":\"snipeout\",\"private\":true,\"type\":\"module\",\"devDependencies\":{\"playwright\":\"1.63.0\"}}' > package.json; npm install --silent 2>&1 | tail -3; ls node_modules | head; grep -n \"50-racing\\|racing\" engine/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md | head; grep -n \"terrain: {\" engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4219,"cache_read_input_tokens":65344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4219},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215","uuid":"814fefc6-4ffc-484f-83cf-3f64ff2e507d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:52.925Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh3aUX7HP8pJH8aPb1sJ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01HvbQBK8TfzVFPLkN3Ehi8E":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184651__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-184651; export TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp; echo '{\"name\":\"snipeout\",\"private\":true,\"type\":\"module\",\"devDependencies\":{\"playwright\":\"1.63.0\"}}' > package.json; npm install --silent 2>&1 | tail -3; ls node_modules | head; grep -n \"50-racing\\|racing\" engine/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md | head; grep -n \"terrain: {\" engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js | head"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HvbQBK8TfzVFPLkN3Ehi8E","type":"tool_result","content":"playwright\nplaywright-core\n456:**Kart racing (Super Mario Kart, F-Zero).** Start from the KART slice (the mode7 and drive modules).\n457:- The track is a TileMap: its walls bounce the karts, its floor tags (`grass`, `sand`, `boost`, ...) slow or boost them (`E.Car`'s `surfaces`), and `E.Mode7({ floor: (x, y) => [r, g, b] })` draws it from the same cells. The racing line is a closed `E.Path` through the track's middle: `E.Race({ path, laps: 3 })` counts laps through its checkpoints in order (a shortcut counts nothing), gives places, and drives every car not a player's (`race.add(car, { input })` for a player, `{ ai: { skill } }` for the rest).\n461:**Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Hang-On).** Start from the ROAD slice (the road module).\n465:**Top-down racing and driving (Micro Machines, RC Pro-Am, GTA).** `E.Car` on a TileMap in the `topdown` view: the same cars, laps and drivers as the kart (`E.Race`), drawn from above (a box of `px.poly` on `r.w()` corner points, turned by `car.angle`); GTA's car is a `E.Car` the hero gets into (`kart: false`: drift is a handbrake).\n564:**3D kart racing (Mario Kart 64, Crash Team Racing).** The 3D RACING kit (the drive module). The circuit is a `world.track` along a closed `E.Path` with heights (banked bends, a hill, a hump to jump, boost `pads`, `gaps` in its walls where a shortcut, a track of its own with `surface: 'dirt'`, leaves and rejoins); karts are `world.vehicle({ kind: 'kart', rig })` raced by `E.Race` (`race.update(dt, null)`: laps, places, its drivers, items); the camera `'behind'` each; set a kart that has left the course back on the road after a moment (Lakitu); two players through `game.splitScreen(2)` and `world.addCamera`.\n646:**Real 3D**: `dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js` puts a three.js and Rapier world under a game (make the game with `bg: null`); its header is its manual, with a complete game. Its kits, `dist/kits/my-3d2dge-3d-<action|platformer|shooter|horror|racing|flight|crawler>.html`, are served, not opened from a disk (they load `vendor/`); the handoff package leaves them out. `docs/ENGINE-3D.md` says how it fits the engine.\n205:## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\n206:terrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\n864: * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n2222:    if (!o.terrain && (!o.level || !o.level.rows)) throw new Error('my-3D2dge 3D: new E.World3D(game, { level: { rows: [...], legend: {...} } }) needs a level written as text (or { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } }: an open world)');","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215","uuid":"18bbb01c-51d0-49a6-97fe-c4d60cba4b8d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:47:53.447Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"playwright\nplaywright-core\n456:**Kart racing (Super Mario Kart, F-Zero).** Start from the KART slice (the mode7 and drive modules).\n457:- The track is a TileMap: its walls bounce the karts, its floor tags (`grass`, `sand`, `boost`, ...) slow or boost them (`E.Car`'s `surfaces`), and `E.Mode7({ floor: (x, y) => [r, g, b] })` draws it from the same cells. The racing line is a closed `E.Path` through the track's middle: `E.Race({ path, laps: 3 })` counts laps through its checkpoints in order (a shortcut counts nothing), gives places, and drives every car not a player's (`race.add(car, { input })` for a player, `{ ai: { skill } }` for the rest).\n461:**Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Hang-On).** Start from the ROAD slice (the road module).\n465:**Top-down racing and driving (Micro Machines, RC Pro-Am, GTA).** `E.Car` on a TileMap in the `topdown` view: the same cars, laps and drivers as the kart (`E.Race`), drawn from above (a box of `px.poly` on `r.w()` corner points, turned by `car.angle`); GTA's car is a `E.Car` the hero gets into (`kart: false`: drift is a handbrake).\n564:**3D kart racing (Mario Kart 64, Crash Team Racing).** The 3D RACING kit (the drive module). The circuit is a `world.track` along a closed `E.Path` with heights (banked bends, a hill, a hump to jump, boost `pads`, `gaps` in its walls where a shortcut, a track of its own with `surface: 'dirt'`, leaves and rejoins); karts are `world.vehicle({ kind: 'kart', rig })` raced by `E.Race` (`race.update(dt, null)`: laps, places, its drivers, items); the camera `'behind'` each; set a kart that has left the course back on the road after a moment (Lakitu); two players through `game.splitScreen(2)` and `world.addCamera`.\n646:**Real 3D**: `dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js` puts a three.js and Rapier world under a game (make the game with `bg: null`); its header is its manual, with a complete game. Its kits, `dist/kits/my-3d2dge-3d-<action|platformer|shooter|horror|racing|flight|crawler>.html`, are served, not opened from a disk (they load `vendor/`); the handoff package leaves them out. `docs/ENGINE-3D.md` says how it fits the engine.\n205:## Open worlds: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } })\n206:terrain: { size (32768: two kilometres), height, color: (x, y, z, nz, out) => [r, g, b] (0..255), cell (32), chunk (32\n864: * 3b. TERRAIN  an open world instead of a level: new E.World3D(game, { terrain: { size, height, color, ... } })\n2222:    if (!o.terrain && (!o.level || !o.level.rows)) throw new Error('my-3D2dge 3D: new E.World3D(game, { level: { rows: [...], legend: {...} } }) needs a level written as text (or { terrain: { height: (x, y) => z, ... } }: an open world)');","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HvbQBK8TfzVFPLkN3Ehi8E","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
