{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh5nx2A7kHAVVqTDxdDk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":305070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215","uuid":"4cad66d0-8ef5-4964-af3c-0bb409791a2a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:16:52.409Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh5nwkH6PYc1jNUxdeFg","thinking_duration_ms":22010,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh5nx2A7kHAVVqTDxdDk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JzhJU34xETD1X5HPEKYQkN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184651__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-184651; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/11-data-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"plan: 'PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)'\",\"plan: 'PLAN.md'\")\ns=s.replace(\"testing: 'Headless Node simulation tests and a Playwright Chromium headless smoke test; screenshots only for what scripts cannot judge; no subagents'\",\"testing: 'Headless tests behind one command (node tests/run.mjs --browser): Node simulation suites with bot players, plus a Playwright Chromium suite on the bundled file that plays every mode, drives the game with a stubbed DualSense and the keyboard, runs attract and a stand-in AI Hub; screenshots only for layout; no subagents'\")\ns=s.replace(\"research: 'None beyond the PLAN, the engine docs and the AI Hub client'\",\"research: 'None beyond PLAN.md, the engine docs and the AI Hub client'\")\nfb={\n\"'TESTING_1'\":\"'Eleven real issues: a syntax error that blocked boot, E.World3D.INPUT read before the 3D add-on loads, craft launched 140 m into the air by a vertical-speed bug, spurious take-offs from slice-edge noise, double lap time on finishing, scratch-frame aliasing in the track queries, Math.random leaking into the sim (found by the replay-hash test), weapons far too lethal for a human, an Academy drill that could soft-lock, a missing font glyph, and keyboard X and B drawn as Xbox buttons.'\",\n\"'TESTING_2'\":\"'Three: the boot-blocking syntax error, the craft launching into the sky, and the Academy weapon drill that could never complete once a weapon was held.'\",\n\"'TESTING_3'\":\"'The Node bot suite: a bot drives every track and class, plus full-grid races whose seeded hash must repeat. It found the sky-launch, the nondeterminism and the lethal weapon balance without anyone looking at a picture.'\",\n\"'TESTING_4'\":\"'The per-weapon fires-once checks: they never failed. Screenshots of menus were also low value apart from the missing glyph and the glyph-chip bug.'\",\n\"'E1'\":\"'The fixed-step loop with game.advance, so whole races, the attract timer and a stand-in hub could be played headless in seconds; the standard pause, settings, rebinding and boot screens; the chip synth with layers; and World3D taking plain three.js meshes in node materials with bloom and the pixel look for free.'\",\n\"'E2'\":\"'Yes. E.World3D does not exist when classic scripts run (the add-on is a deferred module), so E.World3D.INPUT crashed at boot. game.advance right after game.go does not switch scenes until a real frame has passed. audio.sfx has no delay option, so the gibberish voice uses timers.'\",\n\"'E3'\":\"'Track-space hover physics on banked splines with crest air time, the track, craft and scenery mesh builders, the ten weapons and the AI, and the 10-foot menu and glyph kit.'\",\n\"'E4'\":\"'Using World3D as a pure renderer: it wants a level or terrain, so a one-tile pit level stands in; the engine axes (x east, y south, z up) map to three.js with a reflection, which made winding and camera roll signs a matter of trial and error; and the picture could only be checked by screenshots.'\",\n\"'E5'\":\"'One small thing: the button-symbol setting defaults to PlayStation, sits under Display, and offers PlayStation or Xbox. Marked SNIPEOUT EDIT in engine/my-3d2dge.js.'\",\n\"'E6'\":\"'Make E.World3D.INPUT and E.World3D.SETTINGS available before the add-on loads (or load it synchronously), and add a levelless mode for worlds made only of custom meshes.'\",\n\"'P1'\":\"'The plan: pinned versions, axis and unit conventions, the determinism rules, the hub skeleton and the one-command testing rule saved hours and kept the build coherent.'\",\n\"'P2'\":\"'The scale. Four tracks, six songs, split-screen VERSUS, replays, tunnels, gap jumps and eleven drills is more than one session builds, and the plan paths use another run folder name than TASK.md (TASK.md won).'\",\n\"'P3'\":\"'Keeping every built feature complete with no stubs while cutting scope. I cut local split-screen VERSUS, REPLAY, tunnels and gap jumps, and shipped four songs plus stings instead of six.'\",\n\"'P4'\":\"'Mark which plan features are mandatory and which may be cut, shorten the plan, and say whether a plan-driven build may drop plan-only features.'\"}\nfor k,v in fb.items():\n    assert k in s,k; s=s.replace(k,v)\ns=s.replace(\"engineChanges: [\",\"engineChanges: [\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/00-core.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"'Default button symbols are PlayStation (engine default was Auto), so the controller prompts match the DualSense out of the box.' ] };\",\"'Default button symbols are PlayStation (the engine default was Auto), under Display in Settings with an Xbox option, so controller prompts match the DualSense out of the box. Marked SNIPEOUT EDIT in engine/my-3d2dge.js.', 'Not changed: the 3D add-on. The plan also asked for analog buttons, font glyphs and synth extensions in the engine; this build instead reads trigger values straight from the gamepad, draws its own glyph chips and uses the stock chip synth.' ] };\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/95-main.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"E.font.title(g, 'HD', W / 2 + 118,\",\"E.font.title(g, 'HD', W / 2 + 134,\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -c \"TESTING_1\\|'E1'\" src/11-data-about.js; cat > tools/exit-interview.mjs <<'E'\n// Writes ../exit-interview.json from src/11-data-about.js (the same text the About screen shows) and checks it parses.\nimport fs from 'node:fs'; import path from 'node:path'; import { loadSim } from '../tests/lib/load.mjs'; import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nconst root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\nconst SN = loadSim(['00-core', '11-data-about']); const A = SN.ABOUT;\nconst o = { sourceInformation: A.sourceInformation, testingFeedback: A.testingFeedback, engineFeedback: A.engineFeedback, promptFeedback: A.promptFeedback,\n  aiHub: { name: 'SNIPEOUT HD', tagline: 'Anti-gravity. Anti-everyone.', description: 'An anti-gravity combat racer inspired by Wipeout HD: banked roller-coaster tracks, ten weapons, airbrakes and a deadpan league that sponsors everything. Race, snipe, survive Overclock or race ghosts of other players in a hub session.', type: 'Game', genre: 'Racing', source: 'Wipeout HD', series: 'Wipeout', players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Steer A/D or left stick, thrust W or ✕, airbrakes Q/E or L2/R2, fire Space or □, absorb F or ○', tags: ['3d', 'racing', 'sci-fi', 'vehicles', 'low-poly', 'third-person'] } };\nconst file = path.resolve(root, '..', 'exit-interview.json'); fs.writeFileSync(file, JSON.stringify(o, null, 2));\nconst back = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8')); for (const k of Object.keys(back.sourceInformation)) if (!String(back.sourceInformation[k]).trim()) throw new Error('empty ' + k);\nconsole.log('wrote exit-interview.json:', back.testingFeedback.length, back.engineFeedback.length, back.promptFeedback.length, 'answers');\nE\nnode tools/exit-interview.mjs && node tools/bundle.mjs && TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp node tests/run.mjs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":707,"cache_read_input_tokens":305070,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":707},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215","uuid":"69a4b346-2e1d-406f-9ae1-5ea77a7528e2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:17:11.883Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh5nwkH6PYc1jNUxdeFg","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01JzhJU34xETD1X5HPEKYQkN":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261103-184651__xa320fb/work/SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-184651; python3 - <<'E'\np='src/11-data-about.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"plan: 'PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort)'\",\"plan: 'PLAN.md'\")\ns=s.replace(\"testing: 'Headless Node simulation tests and a Playwright Chromium headless smoke test; screenshots only for what scripts cannot judge; no subagents'\",\"testing: 'Headless tests behind one command (node tests/run.mjs --browser): Node simulation suites with bot players, plus a Playwright Chromium suite on the bundled file that plays every mode, drives the game with a stubbed DualSense and the keyboard, runs attract and a stand-in AI Hub; screenshots only for layout; no subagents'\")\ns=s.replace(\"research: 'None beyond the PLAN, the engine docs and the AI Hub client'\",\"research: 'None beyond PLAN.md, the engine docs and the AI Hub client'\")\nfb={\n\"'TESTING_1'\":\"'Eleven real issues: a syntax error that blocked boot, E.World3D.INPUT read before the 3D add-on loads, craft launched 140 m into the air by a vertical-speed bug, spurious take-offs from slice-edge noise, double lap time on finishing, scratch-frame aliasing in the track queries, Math.random leaking into the sim (found by the replay-hash test), weapons far too lethal for a human, an Academy drill that could soft-lock, a missing font glyph, and keyboard X and B drawn as Xbox buttons.'\",\n\"'TESTING_2'\":\"'Three: the boot-blocking syntax error, the craft launching into the sky, and the Academy weapon drill that could never complete once a weapon was held.'\",\n\"'TESTING_3'\":\"'The Node bot suite: a bot drives every track and class, plus full-grid races whose seeded hash must repeat. It found the sky-launch, the nondeterminism and the lethal weapon balance without anyone looking at a picture.'\",\n\"'TESTING_4'\":\"'The per-weapon fires-once checks: they never failed. Screenshots of menus were also low value apart from the missing glyph and the glyph-chip bug.'\",\n\"'E1'\":\"'The fixed-step loop with game.advance, so whole races, the attract timer and a stand-in hub could be played headless in seconds; the standard pause, settings, rebinding and boot screens; the chip synth with layers; and World3D taking plain three.js meshes in node materials with bloom and the pixel look for free.'\",\n\"'E2'\":\"'Yes. E.World3D does not exist when classic scripts run (the add-on is a deferred module), so E.World3D.INPUT crashed at boot. game.advance right after game.go does not switch scenes until a real frame has passed. audio.sfx has no delay option, so the gibberish voice uses timers.'\",\n\"'E3'\":\"'Track-space hover physics on banked splines with crest air time, the track, craft and scenery mesh builders, the ten weapons and the AI, and the 10-foot menu and glyph kit.'\",\n\"'E4'\":\"'Using World3D as a pure renderer: it wants a level or terrain, so a one-tile pit level stands in; the engine axes (x east, y south, z up) map to three.js with a reflection, which made winding and camera roll signs a matter of trial and error; and the picture could only be checked by screenshots.'\",\n\"'E5'\":\"'One small thing: the button-symbol setting defaults to PlayStation, sits under Display, and offers PlayStation or Xbox. Marked SNIPEOUT EDIT in engine/my-3d2dge.js.'\",\n\"'E6'\":\"'Make E.World3D.INPUT and E.World3D.SETTINGS available before the add-on loads (or load it synchronously), and add a levelless mode for worlds made only of custom meshes.'\",\n\"'P1'\":\"'The plan: pinned versions, axis and unit conventions, the determinism rules, the hub skeleton and the one-command testing rule saved hours and kept the build coherent.'\",\n\"'P2'\":\"'The scale. Four tracks, six songs, split-screen VERSUS, replays, tunnels, gap jumps and eleven drills is more than one session builds, and the plan paths use another run folder name than TASK.md (TASK.md won).'\",\n\"'P3'\":\"'Keeping every built feature complete with no stubs while cutting scope. I cut local split-screen VERSUS, REPLAY, tunnels and gap jumps, and shipped four songs plus stings instead of six.'\",\n\"'P4'\":\"'Mark which plan features are mandatory and which may be cut, shorten the plan, and say whether a plan-driven build may drop plan-only features.'\"}\nfor k,v in fb.items():\n    assert k in s,k; s=s.replace(k,v)\ns=s.replace(\"engineChanges: [\",\"engineChanges: [\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/00-core.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"'Default button symbols are PlayStation (engine default was Auto), so the controller prompts match the DualSense out of the box.' ] };\",\"'Default button symbols are PlayStation (the engine default was Auto), under Display in Settings with an Xbox option, so controller prompts match the DualSense out of the box. Marked SNIPEOUT EDIT in engine/my-3d2dge.js.', 'Not changed: the 3D add-on. The plan also asked for analog buttons, font glyphs and synth extensions in the engine; this build instead reads trigger values straight from the gamepad, draws its own glyph chips and uses the stock chip synth.' ] };\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/95-main.js'; s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"E.font.title(g, 'HD', W / 2 + 118,\",\"E.font.title(g, 'HD', W / 2 + 134,\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -c \"TESTING_1\\|'E1'\" src/11-data-about.js; cat > tools/exit-interview.mjs <<'E'\n// Writes ../exit-interview.json from src/11-data-about.js (the same text the About screen shows) and checks it parses.\nimport fs from 'node:fs'; import path from 'node:path'; import { loadSim } from '../tests/lib/load.mjs'; import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nconst root = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..');\nconst SN = loadSim(['00-core', '11-data-about']); const A = SN.ABOUT;\nconst o = { sourceInformation: A.sourceInformation, testingFeedback: A.testingFeedback, engineFeedback: A.engineFeedback, promptFeedback: A.promptFeedback,\n  aiHub: { name: 'SNIPEOUT HD', tagline: 'Anti-gravity. Anti-everyone.', description: 'An anti-gravity combat racer inspired by Wipeout HD: banked roller-coaster tracks, ten weapons, airbrakes and a deadpan league that sponsors everything. Race, snipe, survive Overclock or race ghosts of other players in a hub session.', type: 'Game', genre: 'Racing', source: 'Wipeout HD', series: 'Wipeout', players: '1–4',\n    controls: 'Steer A/D or left stick, thrust W or ✕, airbrakes Q/E or L2/R2, fire Space or □, absorb F or ○', tags: ['3d', 'racing', 'sci-fi', 'vehicles', 'low-poly', 'third-person'] } };\nconst file = path.resolve(root, '..', 'exit-interview.json'); fs.writeFileSync(file, JSON.stringify(o, null, 2));\nconst back = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(file, 'utf8')); for (const k of Object.keys(back.sourceInformation)) if (!String(back.sourceInformation[k]).trim()) throw new Error('empty ' + k);\nconsole.log('wrote exit-interview.json:', back.testingFeedback.length, back.engineFeedback.length, back.promptFeedback.length, 'answers');\nE\nnode tools/exit-interview.mjs && node tools/bundle.mjs && TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp node tests/run.mjs"}}}
