{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh5xrhhTHtJGSk8scaRy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Snipeout HD** is built, but I cut several features the plan asked for, so it is not the full vertical slice the plan described. The tests pass (162, run with `node tests/run.mjs --browser`). I could not test real DualSense hardware, a real AI Hub, or WebGPU. The first two were stubbed, and headless Chromium ran on WebGL 2.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `SnipeoutHD-WipeoutHD-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261103-184651.html` (1.6 MB, single file)\n- `exit-interview.json` (parses; all 15 `sourceInformation` fields are filled)\n- the dev folder with source, tests and tools\n\n## What I cut from the plan\n- Local 2-player split-screen VERSUS.\n- REPLAY mode.\n- Tunnels and gap jumps. Crest jumps and drops remain.\n- Two of the six songs. There are four track songs plus menu, attract and victory tunes.\n- A real hub harness test. The session code is tested only against a stand-in hub.\n\nEverything else TASK.md lists is built, with no stubs. That includes the tracks, weapons, AI, modes, dev mode, attract mode, 10-foot UI and glyphs, touch notice, About screen and hub session.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 18:46:51\n- **Source:** Wipeout HD\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** anti-gravity combat racing (arcade), with survival and combat-points modes. Third-person chase camera (near, far, cockpit), with trackside TV cameras for menus, attract and spectating.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 plus its 3D add-on, three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3 (loaded by the add-on, unused by craft), AI Hub session client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's pixel-resolution 3D look: vertex-coloured low-poly meshes, neon glow with bloom, pixel HUD and fonts.\n- **Animation:** engine fixed-step loop. Craft tilt, roll, banking and camera swing come from physics values.\n- **Audio:** all synthesized with the engine chip synth: layered songs, engine hum, effects, Animalese-style gibberish voice. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-race session (1–4 players) through the vendored client. The game also runs on its own.\n- **Testing:** headless Node bot and simulation suites plus a Playwright Chromium suite on the bundled file; screenshots only for layout; no subagents.\n- **Research:** none beyond PLAN.md, the engine docs and the hub client.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown.\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium.\n- **Usage:** unknown.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** Eleven:\n  - a syntax error that blocked boot;\n  - `E.World3D.INPUT` read before the 3D add-on loads;\n  - craft launched about 140 m into the air by a vertical-speed bug;\n  - false take-offs from noise at track-slice edges;\n  - a doubled lap time on finishing;\n  - scratch-frame aliasing in the track queries;\n  - `Math.random` leaking into the sim, found by the repeat-hash test;\n  - weapons far too lethal for a human;\n  - an Academy drill that could soft-lock;\n  - a missing font glyph;\n  - keyboard X and B drawn as Xbox buttons.\n- **How many were critical?** Three: the boot-blocking syntax error, the sky-launch bug, and the Academy drill soft-lock.\n- **Most helpful test:** the Node bot suite. A bot drives every track and class, and full-grid races must repeat their seeded hash. It caught the sky-launch, the nondeterminism and the weapon balance without anyone looking at a picture.\n- **Least helpful test:** the per-weapon \"fires once\" checks, which never failed. Menu screenshots were also low value beyond the glyph issues.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the fixed-step loop with `game.advance` (whole races, attract and a stand-in hub run headless in seconds); the standard pause, settings, rebinding and boot screens; the chip synth with layers; and World3D accepting plain three.js meshes with bloom.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** yes. `E.World3D` doesn't exist when classic scripts run, so `E.World3D.INPUT` crashed at boot. `game.advance` right after `game.go` doesn't switch scenes until a real frame passes. `audio.sfx` has no delay option, so the voice uses timers.\n- **Most important thing I built:** track-space hover physics on banked splines with crest air time, the mesh builders for track, craft and scenery, the ten weapons and AI, and the 10-foot menu and glyph kit.\n- **Hardest part:** using World3D as a pure renderer. It wants a level or terrain, so a one-tile pit level stands in. The engine axes (x east, y south, z up) map to three.js with a reflection, which made winding and camera-roll signs trial and error. The picture could only be checked by screenshots.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** the button-symbol setting now defaults to PlayStation, sits under Display, and offers PlayStation or Xbox. It is marked `SNIPEOUT EDIT` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`.\n- **One change I'd make:** make `E.World3D.INPUT` and `SETTINGS` available before the add-on loads, and add a levelless mode for custom-mesh worlds.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan's pinned versions, axis and unit conventions, determinism rules and hub skeleton. The one-command testing rule kept the build coherent.\n- **Confusing:** the scale. Four tracks, six songs, split-screen, replays, tunnels and gap jumps is more than one session builds. The plan also uses a different run-folder name than TASK.md (TASK.md won).\n- **Hardest thing:** keeping every built feature complete with no stubs while cutting scope.\n- **What I'd change:** mark which plan features are mandatory and which may be cut, shorten the plan, and say whether a plan-driven build may drop plan-only features."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":895,"cache_read_input_tokens":313748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":895},"output_tokens":835,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215","uuid":"6eda6a7a-181f-4c82-8814-440e21df32d1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:18:57.080Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh5xrRptbsPXWvibGHNV"}
