{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh5z3D1NRiaPVFqo9iwC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The condition holds: everything TASK.md lists is built, and the cuts I reported were plan-only items.\n\n- **Local split-screen VERSUS, REPLAY, tunnels, gap jumps, and the fifth and sixth songs:** these came from PLAN.md, not TASK.md. TASK.md says where the two disagree, TASK.md wins. It asks for dev mode, attract mode, 10-foot controller-first UI, glyph options, the touch notice, an About screen, and hub multiplayer that also lets the game run on its own. All of those are implemented and covered by the 162 passing tests.\n- **Multiplayer:** I read the \"game on its own\" clause as the game running outside the hub, which it does. If it was meant to require local split-screen, that is the one gap, and I did not build it.\n- **My earlier \"stubbed\" wording:** that was loose. The game has no stubs, TODOs or placeholders, and the bundler checks for those words. What I meant was that the hub and the DualSense were stand-ins in the tests, so no real hardware or real hub was exercised.\n\nThe bundled HTML, `exit-interview.json` (parses, every field answered), and the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections are all in place as in my previous reply."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2548,"cache_read_input_tokens":314643,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2548},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215","uuid":"c59cb2bb-0adf-4841-abd3-3c2be20ac5b0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:19:07.065Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh5z2vti4yEtpQEwWXT5"}
