{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UyT2gbCKzyT51Q4tANjxCb","type":"tool_result","content":"233:Split screen: game.splitScreen(2) and world.addCamera(o): viewport i draws through world.cameras[i]; world.project\n2259:    /** cameras: the world's cameras, [0] its camera; world.addCamera(o) adds one (a split screen's viewport i draws\n2400:  addCamera(o = {}) { const c = new Camera3D(this, Object.assign({ far: this.camera.far }, o)); this.cameras.push(c); return c; }\n2897:    // a split screen's viewport (r.viewport, the 2D engine's game.splitScreen) draws through its own camera\n275:- `E.Input.halfKeys(preset, side)` †: a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons in order, and the preset's gamepad codes (Input.halfKeys(Input.SHMUP, 'right') -> fire on . and Numpad 1, bomb on /)\n471:- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n490:- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n501:- `game.splitScreen(n, o = {})` †: split the screen into n viewports (2 to 4; 0 or 1: one screen again), o: { layout: 'auto' (side by side on a wide screen, stacked on a tall one; a grid for 3 or 4) | 'columns' | 'rows' | 'grid', follow: [targets], z: 16, gap: 1 }\n510:- `game.viewports` †: a split screen's viewports ({ i, x, y, w, h, cam, focus(x, y, z), follow(target, { z }): game.splitScreen), or [] on one screen","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215","uuid":"6bb5790b-0f1a-4743-a657-f1b9bedeea01","timestamp":"2026-11-04