{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011mAPhdrgLvDo3RUdCQSFYU","type":"tool_result","content":"- `new E.Game({ camera })`: the camera of every scene without its own (a scene's camera option: the player's zoom, start)\n- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n- `game.nextView(dir = 1)`: cycle through game.views (or every view): bind it to a key for players who like to switch\n- `game.pause(reason = 'player')`: pause the game, saying why ('player' | 'focus' | 'controller' | 'menu': pauseReason); returns true if it paused. The player resumes (Escape, Start, Resume); resume() does it from code\n- `game.players` †: the players: [game.input (player 1), ...the ones who joined (game.allowJoin, game.addPlayer: section 10j)]; each an input with player (1..4), name ('P1'), color (E.PLAYER_COLORS) and device. A game of one: [game.input]\n- `game.removePlayer(p)` †: a player leaves (its input, or its number, 2 to 4); player 1 has the whole keyboard back when no one shares it\n- `game.resetCamera()` †: undo setZoom and rotateView: the scene's own zoom again (camera.start, or camera.tall on a screen held upright; 1 without), no turn. The player's zoom stays (settings.zoom)\n- `game.setZoom(z)` †: camera zoom on top of the view: game.setZoom(1.5) (.5 .. 3), the game's own; where the scene lets the player zoom (camera.zoom), theirs multiplies it (game.zoom is the two together). Characters, maps, props, particles and lights are drawn by code, so they re-rasterize crisply at the new size; HUD text and \n- `game.shake(a)`: shake the screen by a (pixels, decaying; at most 10 in all); none when reduceMotion, scaled by the player's settings.shake\n3662: *    viewport.focus), the scene drawn once in each (r.viewport says which: { i, x, y, w, h }) and scene.hud(r) once over\n3780:// the dividers, the scene's hud(r) over the whole screen and the frame's own overlays (notes, pause, fades)\n3791:  if (sc && sc.hud) sc.hud(r);\n10520:      if (this.o.hud && this.p) {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a73e9f9c-f8ef-4903-be97-67cc0d869215","uuid":"cee1deaf-f73f-4b0b-ba67-fa326125ef27","timestamp":"2026-11-04T02:19:50.465Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `new E.Game({ camera })`: the camera of every scene without its own (a scene's camera option: the player's zoom, start)\n- `game.addPlayer(o = {})` †: a player in now: { pad: index } (a gamepad) or { keys: 'right' } (the keyboard's right half; player 1 takes the left). Returns its input (null when four play already)\n- `game.allowJoin(o = {})` †: let players join, up to max (2..4): Start on a gamepad no one holds, or 2 on the keyboard (o.keys: false not); onJoin (input, number) as each does. allowJoin(false) closes it (the names split and join are String's and Array's)\n- `game.flash(color = '#ffffff', seconds = .12, strength = 1)`: flash the whole screen with a color for `seconds` (dithered fade out): hits, explosions, lightning. Shorter when reduceMotion, dimmer by the player's settings.flashes\n- `game.nextView(dir = 1)`: cycle through game.views (or every view): bind it to a key for players who like to switch\n- `game.pause(reason = 'player')`: pause the game, saying why ('player' | 'focus' | 'controller' | 'menu': pauseReason); returns true if it paused. The player resumes (Escape, Start, Resume); resume() 